# resources/.gitignore — everything generated or fetched under resources/ is
# reproducible and stays out of git. What SHIPS and stays tracked: the
# *-body.tex bodies and *.tex wrappers, the *2tex.py converters, the *.mk
# includes, the Makefile, and the committed flat SOURCES (*-src.html, *.htm,
# the curated *-thml.xml, and the docs-src/ and catena-src/ trees including
# their source PDFs). The published root PDFs now live in ../docs/. Rebuild
# the rest: the *-fetch targets, then `make body` and `make pdf`.

# LaTeX + Python intermediates (anywhere under resources/)
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
__pycache__/
npnf211.txt
docs-src/bor.txt

# Every TOP-LEVEL intermediate PDF. The leading slash anchors this to
# resources/ itself, so subdirectory SOURCE pdfs (catena-src/*.pdf,
# docs-src/*.pdf) are NOT matched and stay tracked.
/*.pdf

# The complete Schaff corpus: the raw CCEL volume XML (re-fetch with
# `make schaff-fetch`) is reproducible. These volume-id patterns do not touch
# the curated *-thml.xml sources, which are tracked.
anf*.xml
npnf*.xml
hcc*.xml
creeds*.xml

# Multi-file remote source trees for the high-church, Roman, Newman, Summa,
# Second-Temple, and classics waves — reproducible (fetch URLs live in each
# converter's header, e.g. `python classics2tex.py fetch`).
hooker-src/
bcp1559-src/
bcp1662-src/
bcp1928-src/
concord-src/
gibbon-src/
thayer-src/
summa-src/
newman-src/
classics-src/
philo-src/
jubilees-src/
